{"c":[{"id":"b6ef750a1098cf99","sum":"B22: tasks bind to their host connection, revoked when it closes or on any pause, stop, take over or settings change; executor asks Helper.authorize before each act; evals call helper.hostConnected(id). Return in a field presses the default button, unreported.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"563c0e5f60870996","sum":"Return in a frontmost single-line field presses the default button (5/5), and B21's reader does not report it. B22: each consumer connection is a host session; tasks are revoked when it closes; in-process evals playing the host call helper.hostConnected(id).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T031707Z-b7d2054c5f965771","text":"AppKit presses a window's default button on Return typed into a single-line text field: frontmost fixture, Note focused, Send ran 5 of 5. B21's reader counts no Return while a text field has focus (brief), so that submit goes unreported (gui/keys-front).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150809Z-35454632bb9daf62","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the one that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id) or no skill runs on its own.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"648a97f969b90b5d","sum":"B22: any pause, stop, take over, settings/permission/skill/memory change or host disconnect revokes the act grant; the executor asks Helper.authorize before each write, press, raise and calendar add. Tasks bind to their host session; evals call helper.hostConnected(id).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150824Z-0b7169f06df102c4","text":"B22: every pause, take over, stop, Caret pause, settings/permission/skill/memory change and host disconnect revokes the act grant at once (Executor.revoke/recheck); the executor also asks Helper.authorize right before each write, press, raise and calendar add.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150829Z-581618fb20568b53","text":"B22: each consumer connection is a host session; accepted tasks bind to the session that started them and are revoked when it closes; runs with no Tab need a connected host. In-process tests and evals that play the host must call helper.hostConnected(id).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c52def503bedc2af","sum":"B22: mutation tests use --build-path /tmp and grep 'recorded an issue'; --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only; press only whole SAFE_PRESSES labels, never in system prompts (change both lists + press-risk.json). Rig VM display is 2x pixels.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5df295da363b0505","sum":"B22: run mutation swift tests with --build-path /tmp/... and grep 'recorded an issue' (Swift Testing failures). --act-pids needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only and caret-fixture pids; window ids are opaque to the helper.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150830Z-a3b40432646c1572","text":"B22: swift test --build-path /tmp/... keeps mutation runs out of .build/debug; Swift Testing marks failures 'recorded an issue', not ✘, so grep that when checking a mutation was caught.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T150830Z-cd56cc67608f9643","text":"B22: --act-pids now needs CARET_SCREEN_FIXTURE_ACTS=fixture-only and caret-fixture pids; window ids are <pid>-<start µs>-<generation>-<n>, opaque to the helper.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6f5c7126a4148883","sum":"B22: presses only whole labels in SAFE_PRESSES/RiskTable.safePresses, never in system prompts; change both lists and press-risk.json together. Rig VM display is pixels at 2x (use 3840x2400 for panels); close fixture forms >=3 s after a routine run.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T150843Z-b8f6b3671dd764ee","text":"B22: presses only whole labels in risk.ts SAFE_PRESSES / RiskTable.safePresses, never in a system prompt (subrole AXSystemDialog or AXSystemFloatingWindow, or a TCC/SecurityAgent process); change both lists and press-risk.json together.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T162636Z-ec02bde9a2237805","text":"Rig VM display file is pixels at 2x: 1920x1200 gives a 960x600-pt screen, too small for Caret's panels beside caret-fixture forms; A16's drawn walk uses 3840x2400. Close fixture forms >=3 s after a routine run or the bundle loses a copy and scores a miss.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
